":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.0454060635385301,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.04514625454187371,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.005409178153899843,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.027320001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"F&G Annuities & Life, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides annuity and life insurance products in the United States. It offers fixed indexed annuities registered index-linked annuities, pension risk transfer and indexed universal life, and multi-year guarantee annuities; immediate annuities; indexed universal life insurance; pension risk transfer solutions; and institutional funding agreements. The company distributes its products through independent agents, banks, and broker-dealers to retail annuity and life customers, as well as institutional clients. The company was founded in 1959 and is headquartered in Des Moines, Iowa. F&G Annuities & Life, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Fidelity National Financial, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Conor Ernan Murphy C.A., CPA, F.C.A. | CEO & President | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $4.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 35%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $26K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["F&G Annuities & Life, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.1B market cap on $5.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +35% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Net dilution runs at 4.5% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 39% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.38821554169965555},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 69% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"F&G Annuities (FG) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/f-g-annuities-fg-q3-184510000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793990958.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"F&G targets $1B-$1.5B in full-year PRT sales while strategic review of Peak Altitude remains active (NYSE:FG)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668429-f-and-g-targets-1b-1_5b-in-full-year-prt-sales-while-strategic-review-of-peak-altitude","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793988994.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"F&G Annuities & Life raises dividend by 4% to $0.26 (NYSE:FG)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668063-fg-annuities-life-raises-dividend-by-4-to-026","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793969316.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"F&G Annuities & Life, Inc. (FG) Beats Q3 Earnings Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025113/f-g-annuities-life-inc-fg-beats-q3-earnings-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3025113","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793923207.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"F&G Annuities & Life Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/62982604/fg-annuities-life-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977477.0,